<title>COLOMBIA: Nissho Iwai in Colombian hospital deal.</title>
<headline>Nissho Iwai in Colombian hospital deal.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Nissho Iwai Corp has been awarded a $6.7 million contract to upgrade medical equipment at seven hospitals in Colombia's five biggest cities, a statement from the Colombian embassy in Tokyo said.</p>
<p>It said seven Japanese companies bid for the contract, which will involve work in Bogota, Cali, Medellin, Cartagena and Barranquilla, but that Nissho Iwai came in with the lowest offer.</p>
<p>The contract was signed Tuesday in Tokyo, the embassy statement said, adding that it was awarded under terms of the Japanese government's Official Development Assistance program of aid to developing countries.</p>
<p>((-- Tom Brown, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
